WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.631
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:08.631 --> 00:00:14.931
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:24.281
Blackjack: beat the dealer
Watch all four hands from N. This room has Player Dealer enabled, with E dealing first. Beat the dealer without going over 21.

00:00:24.281 --> 00:00:31.930
Rule card: start with 1,000 chips. The default house game lasts eight hands and stands on all 17s. Player Dealer lasts two rotations: four hands with two seats.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:41.280
Choose an amount, then place the bet
Click the 100 chip, or adjust with − / +, then click Bet. The dealer does not bet; other pending amounts stay hidden until the deal.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:48.930
Bet 10–200 in steps of 10, within your stack. Aces count as 1 or 11; J, Q and K count as 10.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:59.380
Split equal-value cards
N has two eights. Click Split to stake another 100 and create two hands. Play the highlighted hand first, then the next.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:07.930
One split per seat, including unequal ranks worth ten. Split aces receive one card each; a split 21 is not a natural blackjack.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:21.929
Double while holding two cards
The first hand totals 11. Click Double to add an equal stake, receive exactly one card, and finish that hand. Doubling after splitting is allowed.

00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:33.929
A hit adds both opportunity and risk
The second hand now acts with 10 points. Click Hit for one card, then reassess. Going over 21 immediately busts the hand.

00:01:33.929 --> 00:01:45.929
Stand to keep your total
The second hand has 19. Click Stand to finish. Only after all player hands finish does the dealer reveal its hole card and act.

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:55.829
The revealed hole card completes the dealer total
E’s hole card is now public: the dealer has 16 and must hit. Once the dealer finishes, each split hand is settled separately.

00:01:55.829 --> 00:02:03.928
A regular win profits 1× the stake; ties return it. A natural two-card 21 profits 1.5×. A player bust loses even if the dealer busts.

00:02:03.928 --> 00:02:14.928
N deals the next hand
E is now the bettor and chooses to stand after betting. N is the dealer and can see its own hole card; E still cannot.

00:02:14.928 --> 00:02:23.928
Rule card: with an ace or ten-value up card, the dealer checks for blackjack first. Dealer blackjack ends the hand immediately. There is no insurance or surrender.

00:02:23.928 --> 00:02:35.928
A player dealer uses the controls too
After E finishes, N has a dealer total of 14. Click Hit. A player dealer cannot stand below 17.

00:02:35.928 --> 00:02:45.828
A player dealer may stand from 17
N has reached 17. Click Stand to finish the dealer turn. Player dealers may also hit at 17 or above; 21 or a bust ends the turn automatically.

00:02:45.828 --> 00:02:53.928
Rule card: no dealer draw is needed if every player hand is busted or a natural. If a player dealer cannot pay all winnings, winners receive proportional payouts.

00:02:53.928 --> 00:03:06.928
Hand three: a natural blackjack
E deals again and N bets 100. Watch for immediate settlement: an unsplit ace plus a ten-value card is a natural blackjack.

00:03:06.928 --> 00:03:14.078
Speed through the last hand
N deals the final hand. E bets, then hits. This accelerated sequence completes the same normal flow until all four hands are settled.

00:03:14.078 --> 00:03:19.927
Below 10 chips a seat cannot bet but still takes its dealer turn. The match ends early if fewer than two seats can bet.

00:03:19.927 --> 00:03:33.934
Four hands complete: compare final stacks
N finishes with 1,250 chips and E with 750. N wins by the final match stack, rather than the last hand alone.
